    },
    {
      "post_id": "580331969709531136",
      "text": "@neilh1983 @flightradar24 hmmm the aircraft climbed to 38,000 then descended at 3000-4000ft per min then sent distress call at 6,800ft",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:34:58 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803314613011661e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580329503932727297",
      "text": "@aeroalexGR You're telling me a decent into an airport approach at 3/4000ft is standard? You'd better do some research matey.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:25:10 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803286910765957e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580425275047063552",
      "text": "@SasCaptain also heading of plane kept constant 26 degrees during last minutes.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 17:45:44 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803299454293852e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580326339460358146",
      "text": "@IgnacioZippy @flightradar24 Emergency descent is about 4,000ft/min in that aircraft yeah. It's not \"standard\" for an airport approach.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:12:35 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803261896650179e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580332979093934080",
      "text": "@SasCaptain @flightradar24 The squawk doesn't show any sign of Mayday, could have been only vocal",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:38:58 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803299454293852e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580330525413531648",
      "text": "@athletespw Thanks.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:29:13 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803302145443144e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580326366609960960",
      "text": "@flightradar24 CNN discussing this right now.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:12:42 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803257990787932e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580329945429385216",
      "text": "@flightradar24 Well- in my opinion it's rather steep. And this is a long time before the approach in DUS. Any MAYDAY call?",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:26:55 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803257990787932e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580330208500277248",
      "text": "@SasCaptain @flightradar24 Yes they did ( french media )",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:27:58 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803299454293852e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580330164418191360",
      "text": "@flightradar24 Not really",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:27:47 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803257990787932e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580329782409297920",
      "text": "@danieljaws93 initial descent rate usually passes -3000fpm",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:26:16 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803295039327273e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580337524188557312",
      "text": "@neilh1983 all I saw was that ATC \"received\" the distress call at 6,800 ft. Utterly baffling",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:57:02 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803364064023224e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580332631822336000",
      "text": "@SasCaptain @flightradar24 The plane had issued a distress call at 10:47 (09:47 GMT), according to sources quoted by AFP news agency.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:37:36 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803299454293852e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580328691076595712",
      "text": "@danieljaws93 You're wrong, I've sat in the cockpit many times and we have exceeded -3000fpm... it is normal, but not throughout",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:21:56 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803259446044344e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580326707908907008",
      "text": "Flight 4U9525 was descending at a rate of about 3000-4000 feet per minute, which is quite standard for an airport approach - @flightradar24",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:14:03 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803257990787932e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580326621988548608",
      "text": "@flightradar24 it's about right for engine out glide too. 38000 is very high for an A320. I'm thinking pressurization failure and passed out",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:13:43 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803257990787932e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580336406402322432",
      "text": "@mattnobby @flightradar24 No need to apologise just as confused as anyone! As far as I heard contact was lost at 6800ft",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:52:36 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803360198301164e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580412174767636480",
      "text": "@SasCaptain @flightradar24 So they were wrong, they did not use MAYDAY at anytime... Marseille controler",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 16:53:40 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.80330473940992e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580337869501440000",
      "text": "@mattnobby Wow - that is strange. not heard that yet so thank you. Adds another layer of mystery",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:58:24 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803375241885573e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580326421463240704",
      "text": "@danieljaws93 @flightradar24 ok, thanks",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:12:55 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803263394603581e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580332129806082048",
      "text": "@SasCaptain @flightradar24 yes there was a mayday apparently but no 770 squawk",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:35:36 +0000 2015",
